From 7af682c6d0322dfe24dd7ce102330d9c69d6c144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:43:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/23] demux: ps: carry the whole track across a PSM version
 change

When a program stream map announces a new version, each configured track
is rebuilt into a stack ps_track_t and assigned over the live one. Only
fmt is initialised there, and ps_track_fill() fills in just i_skip, i_id
and fmt, so i_next_block_flags, i_first_pts and i_last_pts are
indeterminate when the structure is copied.

es is repaired on the line above; those three are not. DEMUX_GET_TIME
subtracts i_first_pts from the current timestamp and DEMUX_SET_TIME uses
it to build the ratio it forwards to DEMUX_SET_POSITION, so a seek lands
anywhere and the reported time is meaningless. The SCR heuristic in
Demux() can also latch on the result and disable its own timing path.

The track is the same elementary stream either way - only its format
changed - so carry those fields over.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h b/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h
index 8136cb6044..567cdb973e 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h
+++ b/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h
@@ -750,6 +750,14 @@ static inline int ps_psm_fill( ps_psm_t *p_psm,
         tk_tmp.b_configured = true;
         tk_tmp.b_updated = true;
         tk_tmp.es = tk[i].es;
+        /* Carry the rest of the track over. This is the same elementary
+         * stream, only its format has changed, and ps_track_fill() only
+         * fills in i_skip, i_id and fmt. Without this the assignment below
+         * copies indeterminate values into the live track, which
+         * DEMUX_GET_TIME and DEMUX_SET_TIME go on to read. */
+        tk_tmp.i_next_block_flags = tk[i].i_next_block_flags;
+        tk_tmp.i_first_pts = tk[i].i_first_pts;
+        tk_tmp.i_last_pts = tk[i].i_last_pts;
         es_format_Clean( &tk[i].fmt );
         tk[i] = tk_tmp;
     }
